        "language": "english",
        "review": "I liked Employee 925. The way I interpreted it, it's a mediation on the obscene and dehumanising nature of corporate culture. \nIt's a short (4 endings) Stanley-Parable-esque game with less ah-ah humour and more of a lowkey sense of dread that slowly builds up (but just as equally sarcastic). \nSomehow, it reminded me of the show Severance; you are basically tasked with something nonsensical for the purpose of upholding some HR-speak abstract value that is deprived of its original meaning (e.g. you're communicating with another employee via Morse code to train 'active listening').\n\nI'm curious to see what game Eiras does next",
